+     * earlier, because they are closed already.
+     *
+     * So publication moves out of the guest rather than being retried in it.
+     * The finished cache is renamed to `<final>.ready`, a name nothing ever
+     * opens or maps, so that rename always succeeds -- and the host promotes it
+     * before the next session starts anything, where a plain Linux rename(2)
+     * replaces a mapped file without complaint because wineserver is not
+     * involved. See fexCachePromote in SessionRuntime.kt.
+     *
+     * `.ready` rather than leaving `.new` in place, because the two states must
+     * be told apart: `.new` is also what a compiler killed mid-write leaves
+     * behind, and promoting one of those would publish a truncated cache. Only
+     * `.ready` is ever promoted, and only this line -- after SaveData returned
